#. type: Title =
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "git-send-email(1)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:5
#, no-wrap
msgid "NAME"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:7
msgid "git-send-email - Send a collection of patches as emails"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:10
#, no-wrap
msgid "SYNOPSIS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:16
msgid ""
"'git send-email' [<options>] (<file>|<directory>)...  'git send-email' "
"[<options>] <format-patch-options> 'git send-email' --dump-aliases 'git "
"send-email' --translate-aliases"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:19
#, no-wrap
msgid "DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:26
msgid ""
"Takes the patches given on the command line and emails them out.  Patches "
"can be specified as files, directories (which will send all files in the "
"directory), or directly as a revision list.  In the last case, any format "
"accepted by linkgit:git-format-patch[1] can be passed to `git send-email`, "
"as well as options understood by linkgit:git-format-patch[1]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:30
msgid ""
"The header of the email is configurable via command-line options.  If not "
"specified on the command line, the user will be prompted with a ReadLine "
"enabled interface to provide the necessary information."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:32
msgid "There are two formats accepted for patch files:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:34
msgid "mbox format files"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:37
msgid ""
"This is what linkgit:git-format-patch[1] generates.  Most headers and MIME "
"formatting are ignored."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:40
msgid ""
"The original format used by Greg Kroah-Hartman's `send_lots_of_email.pl` "
"script"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:43
msgid ""
"This format expects the first line of the file to contain the `Cc:` value "
"and the `Subject:` of the message as the second line."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:46
#, no-wrap
msgid "OPTIONS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ~
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:49
#, no-wrap
msgid "Composing"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:51
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--annotate`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:55
msgid ""
"Review and edit each patch you're about to send. Default is the value of "
"`sendemail.annotate`. See the CONFIGURATION section for "
"`sendemail.multiEdit`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:56
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--bcc=<address>,...`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:59
msgid ""
"Specify a `Bcc:` value for each email. Default is the value of "
"`sendemail.bcc`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:61
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:67
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:144
msgid "This option may be specified multiple times."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:62
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--cc=<address>,...`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:65
msgid ""
"Specify a starting `Cc:` value for each email.  Default is the value of "
"`sendemail.cc`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:68
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--compose`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:71
msgid ""
"Invoke a text editor (see GIT_EDITOR in linkgit:git-var[1])  to edit an "
"introductory message for the patch series."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:78
msgid ""
"When `--compose` is used, `git send-email` will use the `From`, `To`, `Cc`, "
"`Bcc`, `Subject`, `Reply-To`, and `In-Reply-To` headers specified in the "
"message. If the body of the message (what you type after the headers and a "
"blank line) only contains blank (or `Git:` prefixed) lines, the summary "
"won't be sent, but the headers mentioned above will be used unless they are "
"removed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:80
msgid "Missing `From` or `In-Reply-To` headers will be prompted for."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:82
msgid "See the CONFIGURATION section for `sendemail.multiEdit`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:83
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--from=<address>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:90
msgid ""
"Specify the sender of the emails.  If not specified on the command line, the "
"value of the `sendemail.from` configuration option is used.  If neither the "
"command-line option nor `sendemail.from` are set, then the user will be "
"prompted for the value.  The default for the prompt will be the value of "
"`GIT_AUTHOR_IDENT`, or `GIT_COMMITTER_IDENT` if that is not set, as returned "
"by `git var -l`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:91
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--reply-to=<address>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:95
msgid ""
"Specify the address where replies from recipients should go to.  Use this if "
"replies to messages should go to another address than what is specified with "
"the `--from` parameter."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:96
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--in-reply-to=<identifier>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:102
msgid ""
"Make the first mail (or all the mails with `--no-thread`) appear as a reply "
"to the given Message-ID, which avoids breaking threads to provide a new "
"patch series.  The second and subsequent emails will be sent as replies "
"according to the `--[no-]chain-reply-to` setting."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:106
msgid ""
"So for example when `--thread` and `--no-chain-reply-to` are specified, the "
"second and subsequent patches will be replies to the first one like in the "
"illustration below where `[PATCH v2 0/3]` is in reply to `[PATCH 0/2]`:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:114
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  [PATCH 0/2] Here is what I did...\n"
"    [PATCH 1/2] Clean up and tests\n"
"    [PATCH 2/2] Implementation\n"
"    [PATCH v2 0/3] Here is a reroll\n"
"      [PATCH v2 1/3] Clean up\n"
"      [PATCH v2 2/3] New tests\n"
"      [PATCH v2 3/3] Implementation\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:117
msgid ""
"Only necessary if `--compose` is also set.  If `--compose` is not set, this "
"will be prompted for."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:118
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--outlook-id-fix`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:119
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--no-outlook-id-fix`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:122
msgid ""
"Microsoft Outlook SMTP servers discard the Message-ID sent via email and "
"assign a new random Message-ID, thus breaking threads."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:127
msgid ""
"With `--outlook-id-fix`, `git send-email` uses a mechanism specific to "
"Outlook servers to learn the Message-ID the server assigned to fix the "
"threading. Use it only when you know that the server reports the rewritten "
"Message-ID the same way as Outlook servers do."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:131
msgid ""
"Without this option specified, the fix is done by default when talking to "
"'smtp.office365.com' or 'smtp-mail.outlook.com'. Use `--no-outlook-id-fix` "
"to disable even when talking to these two servers."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:132
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--subject=<string>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:136
msgid ""
"Specify the initial subject of the email thread.  Only necessary if "
"`--compose` is also set.  If `--compose` is not set, this will be prompted "
"for."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:137
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--to=<address>,...`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:142
msgid ""
"Specify the primary recipient of the emails generated. Generally, this will "
"be the upstream maintainer of the project involved. Default is the value of "
"the `sendemail.to` configuration value; if that is unspecified, and "
"`--to-cmd` is not specified, this will be prompted for."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:145
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--8bit-encoding=<encoding>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:151
msgid ""
"When encountering a non-ASCII message or subject that does not declare its "
"encoding, add headers/quoting to indicate it is encoded in <encoding>.  "
"Default is the value of the `sendemail.assume8bitEncoding`; if that is "
"unspecified, this will be prompted for if any non-ASCII files are "
"encountered."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:153
msgid "Note that no attempts whatsoever are made to validate the encoding."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:154
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--compose-encoding=<encoding>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:157
msgid ""
"Specify encoding of compose message. Default is the value of the "
"`sendemail.composeEncoding`; if that is unspecified, UTF-8 is assumed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:158
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--transfer-encoding=(7bit|8bit|quoted-printable|base64|auto)`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:166
msgid ""
"Specify the transfer encoding to be used to send the message over SMTP.  "
"`7bit` will fail upon encountering a non-ASCII message. `quoted-printable` "
"can be useful when the repository contains files that contain carriage "
"returns, but makes the raw patch email file (as saved from an MUA) much "
"harder to inspect manually. `base64` is even more fool proof, but also even "
"more opaque. `auto` will use `8bit` when possible, and `quoted-printable` "
"otherwise."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:169
msgid ""
"Default is the value of the `sendemail.transferEncoding` configuration "
"value; if that is unspecified, default to `auto`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:170
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--xmailer`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:171
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--no-xmailer`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:175
msgid ""
"Add (or prevent adding) the `X-Mailer:` header.  By default, the header is "
"added, but it can be turned off by setting the `sendemail.xmailer` "
"configuration variable to `false`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ~
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:177
#, no-wrap
msgid "Sending"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:179
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--envelope-sender=<address>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:187
msgid ""
"Specify the envelope sender used to send the emails.  This is useful if your "
"default address is not the address that is subscribed to a list. In order to "
"use the `From` address, set the value to `auto`. If you use the `sendmail` "
"binary, you must have suitable privileges for the `-f` parameter.  Default "
"is the value of the `sendemail.envelopeSender` configuration variable; if "
"that is unspecified, choosing the envelope sender is left to your MTA."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:188
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--sendmail-cmd=<command>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:195
msgid ""
"Specify a command to run to send the email. The command should be "
"sendmail-like; specifically, it must support the `-i` option.  The command "
"will be executed in the shell if necessary.  Default is the value of "
"`sendemail.sendmailCmd`.  If unspecified, and if `--smtp-server` is also "
"unspecified, `git send-email` will search for `sendmail` in `/usr/sbin`, "
"`/usr/lib` and `$PATH`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:196
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--smtp-encryption=<encryption>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:209
msgid ""
"Specify in what way encrypting begins for the SMTP connection.  Valid values "
"are `ssl` and `tls`. Any other value reverts to plain (unencrypted) SMTP, "
"which defaults to port 25.  Despite the names, both values will use the same "
"newer version of TLS, but for historic reasons have these names. `ssl` "
"refers to \"implicit\" encryption (sometimes called SMTPS), that uses port "
"465 by default.  `tls` refers to \"explicit\" encryption (often known as "
"STARTTLS), that uses port 25 by default. Other ports might be used by the "
"SMTP server, which are not the default. Commonly found alternative port for "
"`tls` and unencrypted is 587. You need to check your provider's "
"documentation or your server configuration to make sure for your own "
"case. Default is the value of `sendemail.smtpEncryption`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:210
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--smtp-domain=<FQDN>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:216
msgid ""
"Specifies the Fully Qualified Domain Name (FQDN) used in the HELO/EHLO "
"command to the SMTP server.  Some servers require the FQDN to match your IP "
"address.  If not set, `git send-email` attempts to determine your FQDN "
"automatically.  Default is the value of `sendemail.smtpDomain`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:217
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--smtp-auth=<mechanisms>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:220
msgid ""
"Whitespace-separated list of allowed SMTP-AUTH mechanisms. This setting "
"forces using only the listed mechanisms. Example:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:223
#, no-wrap
msgid "$ git send-email --smtp-auth=\"PLAIN LOGIN GSSAPI\" ...\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:231
msgid ""
"If at least one of the specified mechanisms matches the ones advertised by "
"the SMTP server and if it is supported by the utilized SASL library, the "
"mechanism is used for authentication. If neither `sendemail.smtpAuth` nor "
"`--smtp-auth` is specified, all mechanisms supported by the SASL library can "
"be used. The special value `none` maybe specified to completely disable "
"authentication independently of `--smtp-user`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:232
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--smtp-pass[=<password>]`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:237
msgid ""
"Password for SMTP-AUTH. The argument is optional: If no argument is "
"specified, then the empty string is used as the password. Default is the "
"value of `sendemail.smtpPass`, however `--smtp-pass` always overrides this "
"value."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:243
msgid ""
"Furthermore, passwords need not be specified in configuration files or on "
"the command line. If a username has been specified (with `--smtp-user` or a "
"`sendemail.smtpUser`), but no password has been specified (with "
"`--smtp-pass` or `sendemail.smtpPass`), then a password is obtained using "
"linkgit:git-credential[1]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:244
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--no-smtp-auth`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:246
msgid "Disable SMTP authentication. Short hand for `--smtp-auth=none`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:247
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--smtp-server=<host>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:253
msgid ""
"If set, specifies the outgoing SMTP server to use (e.g.  `smtp.example.com` "
"or a raw IP address).  If unspecified, and if `--sendmail-cmd` is also "
"unspecified, the default is to search for `sendmail` in `/usr/sbin`, "
"`/usr/lib` and `$PATH` if such a program is available, falling back to "
"`localhost` otherwise."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:259
msgid ""
"For backward compatibility, this option can also specify a full pathname of "
"a sendmail-like program instead; the program must support the `-i` option.  "
"This method does not support passing arguments or using plain command "
"names.  For those use cases, consider using `--sendmail-cmd` instead."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:260
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--smtp-server-port=<port>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:267
msgid ""
"Specifies a port different from the default port (SMTP servers typically "
"listen to smtp port 25, but may also listen to submission port 587, or the "
"common SSL smtp port 465); symbolic port names (e.g. `submission` instead of "
"587)  are also accepted. The port can also be set with the "
"`sendemail.smtpServerPort` configuration variable."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:268
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--smtp-server-option=<option>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:272
msgid ""
"If set, specifies the outgoing SMTP server option to use.  Default value can "
"be specified by the `sendemail.smtpServerOption` configuration option."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:276
msgid ""
"The `--smtp-server-option` option must be repeated for each option you want "
"to pass to the server. Likewise, different lines in the configuration files "
"must be used for each option."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:277
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--smtp-ssl`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:279
msgid "Legacy alias for `--smtp-encryption ssl`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:280
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--smtp-ssl-cert-path`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:292
msgid ""
"Path to a store of trusted CA certificates for SMTP SSL/TLS certificate "
"validation (either a directory that has been processed by `c_rehash`, or a "
"single file containing one or more PEM format certificates concatenated "
"together: see the description of the `-CAfile` _<file>_ and the `-CApath` "
"_<dir>_ options of https://docs.openssl.org/master/man1/openssl-verify/ "
"[OpenSSL's verify(1) manual page] for more information on these).  Set it to "
"an empty string to disable certificate verification.  Defaults to the value "
"of the `sendemail.smtpSSLCertPath` configuration variable, if set, or the "
"backing SSL library's compiled-in default otherwise (which should be the "
"best choice on most platforms)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:293
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--smtp-user=<user>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:297
msgid ""
"Username for SMTP-AUTH. Default is the value of `sendemail.smtpUser`; if a "
"username is not specified (with `--smtp-user` or `sendemail.smtpUser`), then "
"authentication is not attempted."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:298
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--smtp-debug=(0|1)`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:302
msgid ""
"Enable (1) or disable (0) debug output. If enabled, SMTP commands and "
"replies will be printed. Useful to debug TLS connection and authentication "
"problems."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:303
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--imap-sent-folder=<folder>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:311
msgid ""
"Some email providers (e.g. iCloud) do not send a copy of the emails sent "
"using SMTP to the `Sent` folder or similar in your mailbox. Use this option "
"to use `git imap-send` to send a copy of the emails to the folder specified "
"using this option. You can run `git imap-send --list` to get a list of valid "
"folder names, including the correct name of the `Sent` folder in your "
"mailbox. You can also use this option to send emails to a dedicated IMAP "
"folder of your choice."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:314
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:328
msgid ""
"This feature requires setting up `git imap-send`. See "
"linkgit:git-imap-send[1] for instructions."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:315
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--use-imap-only`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:316
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--no-use-imap-only`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:324
msgid ""
"If this is set, all emails will only be copied to the IMAP folder specified "
"with `--imap-sent-folder` or `sendemail.imapSentFolder` and will not be sent "
"to the recipients. Useful if you just want to create a draft of the emails "
"and use another email client to send them.  If disabled with "
"`--no-use-imap-only`, the emails will be sent like usual.  Disabled by "
"default, but the `sendemail.useImapOnly` configuration variable can be used "
"to enable it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:329
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--batch-size=<num>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:338
msgid ""
"Some email servers (e.g. 'smtp.163.com') limit the number of emails to be "
"sent per session (connection) and this will lead to a failure when sending "
"many messages.  With this option, send-email will disconnect after sending "
"_<num>_ messages and wait for a few seconds (see `--relogin-delay`) and "
"reconnect, to work around such a limit.  You may want to use some form of "
"credential helper to avoid having to retype your password every time this "
"happens.  Defaults to the `sendemail.smtpBatchSize` configuration variable."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:339
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--relogin-delay=<int>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:343
msgid ""
"Waiting _<int>_ seconds before reconnecting to SMTP server. Used together "
"with `--batch-size` option.  Defaults to the `sendemail.smtpReloginDelay` "
"configuration variable."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ~
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:345
#, no-wrap
msgid "Automating"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:347
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--no-to`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:348
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--no-cc`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:349
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--no-bcc`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:352
msgid "Clears any list of `To:`, `Cc:`, `Bcc:` addresses previously set via config."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:353
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--no-identity`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:356
msgid ""
"Clears the previously read value of `sendemail.identity` set via config, if "
"any."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:357
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--to-cmd=<command>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:362
msgid ""
"Specify a command to execute once per patch file which should generate patch "
"file specific `To:` entries.  Output of this command must be single email "
"address per line.  Default is the value of `sendemail.toCmd` configuration "
"value."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:363
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--cc-cmd=<command>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:368
msgid ""
"Specify a command to execute once per patch file which should generate patch "
"file specific `Cc:` entries.  Output of this command must be single email "
"address per line.  Default is the value of `sendemail.ccCmd` configuration "
"value."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:369
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--header-cmd=<command>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:376
msgid ""
"Specify a command that is executed once per outgoing message and output RFC "
"2822 style header lines to be inserted into them. When the "
"`sendemail.headerCmd` configuration variable is set, its value is always "
"used. When `--header-cmd` is provided at the command line, its value takes "
"precedence over the `sendemail.headerCmd` configuration variable."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:377
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--no-header-cmd`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:379
msgid "Disable any header command in use."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:380
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--chain-reply-to`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:381
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--no-chain-reply-to`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:388
msgid ""
"If this is set, each email will be sent as a reply to the previous email "
"sent.  If disabled with `--no-chain-reply-to`, all emails after the first "
"will be sent as replies to the first email sent.  When using this, it is "
"recommended that the first file given be an overview of the entire patch "
"series. Disabled by default, but the `sendemail.chainReplyTo` configuration "
"variable can be used to enable it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:389
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--identity=<identity>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:394
msgid ""
"A configuration identity. When given, causes values in the "
"`sendemail.<identity>` subsection to take precedence over values in the "
"`sendemail` section. The default identity is the value of "
"`sendemail.identity`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:395
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--signed-off-by-cc`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:396
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--no-signed-off-by-cc`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:401
msgid ""
"If this is set, add emails found in the `Signed-off-by` trailer or `Cc:` "
"lines to the cc list. Default is the value of `sendemail.signedOffByCc` "
"configuration value; if that is unspecified, default to "
"`--signed-off-by-cc`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:402
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--cc-cover`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:403
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--no-cc-cover`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:408
msgid ""
"If this is set, emails found in `Cc:` headers in the first patch of the "
"series (typically the cover letter) are added to the cc list for each email "
"set. Default is the value of `sendemail.ccCover` configuration value; if "
"that is unspecified, default to `--no-cc-cover`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:409
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--to-cover`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:410
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--no-to-cover`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:415
msgid ""
"If this is set, emails found in `To:` headers in the first patch of the "
"series (typically the cover letter) are added to the to list for each email "
"set. Default is the value of `sendemail.toCover` configuration value; if "
"that is unspecified, default to `--no-to-cover`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:416
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--suppress-cc=<category>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:419
msgid "Specify an additional category of recipients to suppress the auto-cc of:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:422
msgid "`author` will avoid including the patch author."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:423
msgid "`self` will avoid including the sender."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:425
msgid ""
"`cc` will avoid including anyone mentioned in Cc lines in the patch header "
"except for self (use `self` for that)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:427
msgid ""
"`bodycc` will avoid including anyone mentioned in Cc lines in the patch body "
"(commit message) except for self (use `self` for that)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:429
msgid ""
"`sob` will avoid including anyone mentioned in the Signed-off-by trailers "
"except for self (use `self` for that)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:432
msgid ""
"`misc-by` will avoid including anyone mentioned in Acked-by, Reviewed-by, "
"Tested-by and other \"-by\" lines in the patch body, except Signed-off-by "
"(use `sob` for that)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:433
msgid "`cccmd` will avoid running the --cc-cmd."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:434
msgid "`body` is equivalent to `sob` + `bodycc` + `misc-by`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:435
msgid "`all` will suppress all auto cc values."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:440
msgid ""
"Default is the value of `sendemail.suppressCc` configuration value; if that "
"is unspecified, default to `self` if `--suppress-from` is specified, as well "
"as `body` if `--no-signed-off-cc` is specified."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:441
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--suppress-from`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:442
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--no-suppress-from`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:446
msgid ""
"If this is set, do not add the `From:` address to the `Cc:` list.  Default "
"is the value of `sendemail.suppressFrom` configuration value; if that is "
"unspecified, default to `--no-suppress-from`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:447
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--thread`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:448
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--no-thread`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:454
msgid ""
"If this is set, the `In-Reply-To` and `References` headers will be added to "
"each email sent.  Whether each mail refers to the previous email (`deep` "
"threading per `git format-patch` wording) or to the first email (`shallow` "
"threading) is governed by `--[no-]chain-reply-to`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:459
msgid ""
"If disabled with `--no-thread`, those headers will not be added (unless "
"specified with `--in-reply-to`).  Default is the value of the "
"`sendemail.thread` configuration value; if that is unspecified, default to "
"`--thread`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:465
msgid ""
"It is up to the user to ensure that no In-Reply-To header already exists "
"when `git send-email` is asked to add it (especially note that `git "
"format-patch` can be configured to do the threading itself).  Failure to do "
"so may not produce the expected result in the recipient's MUA."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:466
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--mailmap`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:467
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--no-mailmap`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:473
msgid ""
"Use the mailmap file (see linkgit:gitmailmap[5]) to map all addresses to "
"their canonical real name and email address. Additional mailmap data "
"specific to `git send-email` may be provided using the "
"`sendemail.mailmap.file` or `sendemail.mailmap.blob` configuration "
"values. Defaults to `sendemail.mailmap`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ~
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:475
#, no-wrap
msgid "Administering"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:477
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--confirm=<mode>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:479
msgid "Confirm just before sending:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:482
msgid "`always` will always confirm before sending."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:483
msgid "`never` will never confirm before sending."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:485
msgid ""
"`cc` will confirm before sending when send-email has automatically added "
"addresses from the patch to the Cc list."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:486
msgid ""
"`compose` will confirm before sending the first message when using "
"--compose."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:487
msgid "`auto` is equivalent to `cc` + `compose`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:492
msgid ""
"Default is the value of `sendemail.confirm` configuration value; if that is "
"unspecified, default to `auto` unless any of the suppress options have been "
"specified, in which case default to `compose`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:493
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--dry-run`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:495
msgid "Do everything except actually send the emails."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:496
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--format-patch`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:497
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--no-format-patch`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:502
msgid ""
"When an argument may be understood either as a reference or as a file name, "
"choose to understand it as a format-patch argument (`--format-patch`)  or as "
"a file name (`--no-format-patch`). By default, when such a conflict occurs, "
"`git send-email` will fail."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:503
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--quiet`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:506
msgid ""
"Make `git send-email` less verbose.  One line per email should be all that "
"is output."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:507
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--validate`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:508
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--no-validate`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:511
msgid ""
"Perform sanity checks on patches.  Currently, validation means the "
"following:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:514
msgid "Invoke the sendemail-validate hook if present (see linkgit:githooks[5])."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:515
msgid "Warn of patches that contain lines longer than"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:519
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"998 characters unless a suitable transfer encoding\n"
"(`auto`, `base64`, or `quoted-printable`) is used;\n"
"this is due to SMTP limits as described by\n"
"https://www.ietf.org/rfc/rfc5322.txt.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:523
msgid ""
"Default is the value of `sendemail.validate`; if this is not set, default to "
"`--validate`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:524
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--force`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:526
msgid "Send emails even if safety checks would prevent it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ~
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:529
#, no-wrap
msgid "Information"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:531
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--dump-aliases`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:536
msgid ""
"Instead of the normal operation, dump the shorthand alias names from the "
"configured alias file(s), one per line in alphabetical order. Note that this "
"only includes the alias name and not its expanded email addresses.  See "
"`sendemail.aliasesFile` for more information about aliases."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:537
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--translate-aliases`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:543
msgid ""
"Instead of the normal operation, read from standard input and interpret each "
"line as an email alias. Translate it according to the configured alias "
"file(s). Output each translated name and email address to standard output, "
"one per line. See `sendemail.aliasFile` for more information about aliases."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:545
#, no-wrap
msgid "CONFIGURATION"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:552
#, no-wrap
msgid "EXAMPLES OF SMTP SERVERS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ~
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:554
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use Gmail as the SMTP Server"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:557
msgid ""
"To use `git send-email` to send your patches through the Gmail SMTP server, "
"edit `~/.gitconfig` to specify your account settings:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:564
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[sendemail]\n"
"\tsmtpEncryption = ssl\n"
"\tsmtpServer = smtp.gmail.com\n"
"\tsmtpUser = yourname@gmail.com\n"
"\tsmtpServerPort = 465\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:570
msgid ""
"Gmail does not allow using your regular password for `git send-email`.  If "
"you have multi-factor authentication set up on your Gmail account, you can "
"generate an app-specific password for use with `git send-email`. Visit "
"https://security.google.com/settings/security/apppasswords to create it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:578
msgid ""
"Alternatively, instead of using an app-specific password, you can use "
"OAuth2.0 authentication with Gmail. OAuth2.0 is more secure than "
"app-specific passwords, and works regardless of whether you have "
"multi-factor authentication set up. `OAUTHBEARER` and `XOAUTH2` are common "
"mechanisms used for this type of authentication. Gmail supports both of "
"them. As an example, if you want to use `OAUTHBEARER`, edit your "
"`~/.gitconfig` file and add `smtpAuth = OAUTHBEARER` to your account "
"settings:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:586
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[sendemail]\n"
"\tsmtpEncryption = ssl\n"
"\tsmtpServer = smtp.gmail.com\n"
"\tsmtpUser = yourname@gmail.com\n"
"\tsmtpServerPort = 465\n"
"\tsmtpAuth = OAUTHBEARER\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:591
msgid ""
"Another alternative is using a tool developed by Google known as "
"https://github.com/google/gmail-oauth2-tools/tree/master/go/sendgmail[sendgmail] "
"to send emails using `git send-email`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ~
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:593
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use Microsoft Outlook as the SMTP Server"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:597
msgid ""
"Unlike Gmail, Microsoft Outlook no longer supports app-specific passwords.  "
"Therefore, OAuth2.0 authentication must be used for Outlook. Also, it only "
"supports `XOAUTH2` authentication mechanism."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:600
msgid ""
"Edit `~/.gitconfig` to specify your account settings for Outlook and use its "
"SMTP server with `git send-email`:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:608
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[sendemail]\n"
"\tsmtpEncryption = tls\n"
"\tsmtpServer = smtp.office365.com\n"
"\tsmtpUser = yourname@outlook.com\n"
"\tsmtpServerPort = 587\n"
"\tsmtpAuth = XOAUTH2\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:611
#, no-wrap
msgid "SENDING PATCHES"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:614
msgid ""
"Once your commits are ready to be sent to the mailing list, run the "
"following commands:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:618
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\t$ git format-patch --cover-letter -M origin/master -o outgoing/\n"
"\t$ edit outgoing/0000-*\n"
"\t$ git send-email outgoing/*\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:621
msgid ""
"The first time you run it, you will be prompted for your credentials.  Enter "
"the app-specific or your regular password as appropriate."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:625
msgid ""
"If you have a credential helper configured (see linkgit:git-credential[1]), "
"the password will be saved in the credential store so you won't have to type "
"it the next time."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:629
msgid ""
"If you are using OAuth2.0 authentication, you need to use an access token in "
"place of a password when prompted. Various OAuth2.0 token generators are "
"available online. Community maintained credential helpers are also "
"available:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:632
msgid ""
"https://github.com/AdityaGarg8/git-credential-email[git-credential-gmail] "
"(cross platform, dedicated helper for authenticating Gmail accounts)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:635
msgid ""
"https://github.com/AdityaGarg8/git-credential-email[git-credential-outlook] "
"(cross platform, dedicated helper for authenticating Microsoft Outlook "
"accounts)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:638
msgid ""
"https://github.com/AdityaGarg8/git-credential-email[git-credential-yahoo] "
"(cross platform, dedicated helper for authenticating Yahoo accounts)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:641
msgid ""
"https://github.com/AdityaGarg8/git-credential-email[git-credential-aol] "
"(cross platform, dedicated helper for authenticating AOL accounts)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:644
msgid ""
"You can also see linkgit:gitcredentials[7] for more OAuth based "
"authentication helpers."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:652
msgid ""
"Proton Mail does not provide an SMTP server to send emails. If you are a "
"paid customer of Proton Mail, you can use "
"https://proton.me/mail/bridge[Proton Mail Bridge] officially provided by "
"Proton Mail to create a local SMTP server for sending emails. For both free "
"and paid users, community maintained projects like "
"https://github.com/AdityaGarg8/git-credential-email[git-protonmail] can be "
"used."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:655
msgid ""
"Note: the following core Perl modules that may be installed with your "
"distribution of Perl are required:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:660
msgid ""
"https://metacpan.org/pod/MIME::Base64[MIME::Base64], "
"https://metacpan.org/pod/MIME::QuotedPrint[MIME::QuotedPrint], "
"https://metacpan.org/pod/Net::Domain[Net::Domain] and "
"https://metacpan.org/pod/Net::SMTP[Net::SMTP]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:662
msgid "These additional Perl modules are also required:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:665
msgid ""
"https://metacpan.org/pod/Authen::SASL[Authen::SASL] and "
"https://metacpan.org/pod/Mail::Address[Mail::Address]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ~
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:667
#, no-wrap
msgid "Exploiting the `sendmailCmd` option of `git send-email`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:675
msgid ""
"Apart from sending emails via an SMTP server, `git send-email` can also send "
"emails through any application that supports sendmail-like commands. You can "
"read documentation of `--sendmail-cmd=<command>` above for more "
"information.  This ability can be very useful if you want to use another "
"application as an SMTP client for `git send-email`, or if your email "
"provider uses proprietary APIs instead of SMTP to send emails."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:679
msgid ""
"As an example, lets see how to configure https://marlam.de/msmtp/[msmtp], a "
"popular SMTP client found in many Linux distributions. Edit `~/.gitconfig` "
"to instruct `git-send-email` to use it for sending emails."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:683
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[sendemail]\n"
"\tsendmailCmd = /usr/bin/msmtp # Change this to the path where msmtp is "
"installed\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:686
msgid "Links of a few such community maintained helpers are:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:689
msgid ""
"https://marlam.de/msmtp/[msmtp] (popular SMTP client with many features, "
"available for Linux and macOS)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:692
msgid ""
"https://github.com/AdityaGarg8/git-credential-email[git-protonmail] (cross "
"platform client that can send emails using the ProtonMail API)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:695
msgid ""
"https://github.com/AdityaGarg8/git-credential-email[git-msgraph] (cross "
"platform client that can send emails using the Microsoft Graph API)"
msgstr ""

